Third-party CONTENT (not code)
------------------------------

Reference material that originates elsewhere — vendor reports, analyst research,
articles, saved web pages, screenshots of other people's documents — is NOT
committed to this repository, whatever its file format.

This is a separate question from the open-source dependencies below, and it runs in
the opposite direction. The dependency question is "may we USE this?". This one is
"may we REPUBLISH this?" — and committing a file to a public repository is
publishing it. A licence to read something is not a licence to redistribute it.

The rule is: learn from a source, then write what you learned in your own words and
cite it. The summary is ours to publish; the source is not.

`scripts/check-publication-boundary.mjs` enforces this. It fails the build on any
reproduced-whole document (PDF, DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, EPUB) with no recorded licence
basis, and on markdown that carries the tell-tale furniture of a scraped web page
(consent banners, CDN asset hosts). It was added after four such files — two
licensed analyst reports and two full page scrapes — were found already committed
here. They have been removed from the tree; note that removal from HEAD does not
remove them from git history.

